commit 565ab1051cb878e189aff2e5a159fd76e101f6b3
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 7 17:07:53 2026 +0000

    Add the sortable list by pointer and keyboard, the second native module (unit Drag 1)
    
    src/browser/drags/ (Drag, createDrag, createDragPlugin, DRAG_EVENTS with
    start, move, and end, each cancelable where the brief says) routes the
    native drag events and keydown from [data-vn-drag] > * to the parent
    host; the move uses Element.moveBefore with insertBefore as the fallback,
    so an item keeps its state and focus; a drop from outside the host, a
    grab outside the handle, and a grab on a control are refused; a live
    region reads the position. The module writes the state attributes
    data-vn-dragging and data-vn-insert and renders nothing; the showcase's
    Native group renders them through Bootstrap utility classes from a
    MutationObserver in Showcase.start. Proofs under Chromium 141 and 153;
    the Escape-during-native-drag reading is a recorded departure.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fwYCgxCd9JhL43kVBLBJV

