+host with `role="list"` and children with `role="listitem"` when the output shares the host.
+The `data-vn-drag` value is reserved for a later group-transfer unit. Drag 1 reads only its
+presence and exchanges nothing between hosts, including hosts whose values match.
+
+Write `draggable="true"` on each item or on its grip handle. The module never adds or removes
+that attribute. A handle limits the grab to that handle and uses the whole item's drag image
+at the grab offset. An `input`, `textarea`, `select`, `button`, `a[href]`, or `contenteditable`
+descendant refuses a grab unless it is the handle. Give an item `tabindex="0"`, or use a
+focusable handle such as a button. This markup supplies a handle and a keyboard focus stop.
+
+```text
+<div data-vn-drag class="list-group" role="list" aria-label="Priorities">
+	<div class="list-group-item" role="listitem">
+		<button type="button" draggable="true" aria-label="Move Review orders">⠿</button>
+		Review orders
+	</div>
+	<div class="list-group-item" role="listitem">
+		<button type="button" draggable="true" aria-label="Move Prepare labels">⠿</button>
+		Prepare labels
+	</div>
+</div>
+```
+
+Alt+ArrowUp and Alt+ArrowDown move the focused item one place without wrapping. A row axis
+uses Alt+ArrowLeft and Alt+ArrowRight. The host's computed flex direction, writing mode, and
+direction determine the axis and its orientation. Other modifiers and composing input leave
+the list alone. Each completed move keeps focus and announces `Moved to position N of M`,
+where `N` is the item's one-based position and `M` counts the authored items.
+
+The pointer path accepts only a session that started in the same host. It sets both transfer
+effects to `move`, writes no payload, and refuses external text and files. The target's midpoint
+chooses the insertion side; `data-vn-insert="before"` or `"after"` changes only when the target
+or side changes. A leave across a nested child keeps the insertion state. A leave out of the host
+clears it. A drop outside, Escape, or a refused move ends without a DOM move.
+
+The host receives these events through the shared `emitEvent` dispatcher.
+
+| Event           | Detail                     | Behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
+| --------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `start.vn.drag` | `item`                     | Fires before a pointer or keyboard grab. Prevention refuses the grab.                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
+| `move.vn.drag`  | `item`, `from`, `to`, `by` | Fires before each DOM move. The indexes are zero-based; `from` is the old index and `to` is the insertion index after removing the item from its old slot. `by` is `pointer` or `keyboard`. Prevention leaves the DOM unchanged, so a data-owning application can prevent and render its own order. |
+| `end.vn.drag`   | `item`, `moved`            | Fires after an admitted session ends, including a refused drop or native `dragend`. `moved` reports whether the controller moved the item.                                                                                                                                                          |
+
+The move uses the platform's state-preserving `moveBefore` method, with `insertBefore` and
+focus restoration when that method is absent. See the [DOM move contract](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-parentnode-movebefore).
+The fallback preserves the node's value and restores focus but cannot promise every state
+preserved by an atomic move. The controller holds no listeners itself: its plugin routes
+`pointerdown`, the native drag events, and `keydown` through the scope. `receive(event, item)`
+is the same input boundary for an explicit `createDrag(host)` consumer that owns routing.
+
+The module writes `data-vn-dragging` on the source and `data-vn-insert` on the target;
+it does not paint those states. A consumer renders them. The showcase's
+`Showcase.start` in `app/browser/Showcase.ts` observes those two attributes on each host
+and toggles Bootstrap utilities on direct-child items: `opacity-50` for the source,
+`border-top border-primary border-2` for `before`, and
+`border-bottom border-primary border-2` for `after`. Removing a state attribute removes
+its utilities. Teardown disconnects each observer. These utility classes already belong to
+the Bootstrap registry admitted by the section proof; the Native group owns no new class family.
+The grip button supplies the affordance. The showcase adds no stylesheet, cursor rule,
+touch-action rule, or style attribute for dragging.
+
+The [module proofs](../tests/src/browser/drags/Drag.test.ts) drive real pointer input and keys,
+read prevention and grab refusals, verify event indexes and position text, and retain an edited
+input's value and focus through `moveBefore`. The [routing proofs](../tests/src/browser/drags/plugins.test.ts)
+read native listener acquisition and release, external and cross-host refusals, a real nested-child
+crossing, and Escape during a native drag. The [purity proof](../tests/src/browser/drags/index.test.ts)
+reads every Bootstrap root source file and pins the Bootstrap plugin order. The
+[factory proof](../tests/src/browser/drags/factories.test.ts) covers configured identity and owned-output
+cleanup. Touch dragging on Android is not established by these desktop Chromium proofs.
+
 ### Native departures
 
-The copy button has no Bootstrap counterpart and no departure from a Bootstrap contract.
+The copy button and sortable list have no Bootstrap counterparts. The sortable list has this
